 "docs": {
  "PICK-ANYWHERE.md": [
   "1: # Pick-anywhere sorting loop (`app/tools/sort_any.py`)",
   "7: ## Run, stop, pause",
   "9: **After the robot was lent out:** `app/tools/resume.sh` brings the stack up in a safe order and refuses if",
   "10: anything else holds the follower port or the cameras. Order: checks, recorders, fresh live frames, hand watchdog,",
   "11: motion server (torque on at the present pose, no motion). `app/tools/resume.sh --go <run name>` also starts the",
   "13: then kill `hand_watch` / `monitor_cams` / `wrist_recorder` by their pid files.",
   "15: Manual start of the loop alone:",
   "19: nohup ../../envs/data-env/bin/python -u -B sort_any.py --run <name> --n 150 --start <k> >> ../../logs/sort_any_<name>.out 2>&1 &",
   "20: touch run/sort_stop     # stop before the next brick (removed automatically)",
   "24: Needed processes (each has a pid file in `run/`; restart only by pid): motion server (`run/mserver/pid`),",
   "25: hand watchdog (`run/hand_watch.pid`), monitor cameras (`run/monitor_cams.pid`), wrist recorder",
   "26: (`run/wrist_recorder.pid`). Start-up runs a check-only jaw check and carries over a brick still in the gripper.",
   "89:   - Cut episodes by the `t_start` / `t_end` in `episode.json`.",
   "105: - **Hand detector**: `app/tools/handdet.py`, one module shared by the watchdog (`hand_watch.py`) and the loop's",
   "114:   - Persistence before a stop: top 1 frame, close 2, wrist 2.",
   "117:     recording; restored to y \u2265 0 with no extra false stop in 2480 recorded frames.",
   "118:   - Labelled check on the 41 e-stop images (16:19\u201318:13Z; labels in `app/tools/tests/fixtures/hand_labels.csv`,",
   "120:     top/close false stop remains. A hand on the laptop off the mat is labelled `hand_outside` and not counted.",
   "121:     The old rules missed a real close-view hand (2993 px) and stopped on mat speckles.",
   "122:   - On 4025 recorded close frames: positives 34 \u2192 8. The 28 removed were all cream-brick false stops, reviewed",
   "124: - The motion server holds the arm on an e-stop and keeps squeezing a held brick.",
   "125: - The loop resumes by itself 3\u20135 s after hands leave. A failed recovery now backs off 1, 2, 4 \u2026 30 s, about",
   "127: - The follower is used only through `/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_5B3D040939-if00`. Torque off",
   "147:   - Arm at `home_closed`, torque off.",
   "148:   - Stopped: loop, motion server, hand watchdog, recorders. No holder on `/dev/ttyACM0` or any `/dev/video*`.",
   "149: - **Hand detector:** `handdet.py`, see Safety. `hand_watch.py` is rewritten on it, with a `main()` and a docstring",
   "151: - **Recovery back-off** in `sort_any.recover()`.",
   "157: - **Dead code removed** from `sort_any.py`: `inspect_pose`, `held_verdict`, `multiview`, `CLOSE_HELD_PX`,",
   "172:   - Evidence report on every episode.",
   "180:   `sort_any.grasp_reachable` replays the approach and descent IK without moving (reach ends at about 296 mm from",
   "192:   segmentation measured on labelled frames. The replay test reports PD-1 without failing on it."
  ],
  "motion_src": [
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:9: The follower port is always the by-id link in so101_motion.FOLLOWER_PORT_BY_ID. The export's",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:16: Limits: every speed is at most 50 units/s (HARD_MAX_SPEED); a larger --max-speed or YAML speed",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:43:     DEFAULT_MAX_SPEED,",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:69:     parser.add_argument(\"--port\", help=\"follower serial port; only the by-id path is accepted (the export's connection_string is ignored)\")",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:71:     parser.add_argument(\"--max-speed\", type=float, default=DEFAULT_MAX_SPEED, help=\"normalized units per second, at most 50\")",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:83:         f\"{'peak_rate':>10} {'peak_accel':>11} {'dwell_s':>7}\"",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:89:             f\"{row['duration_s']!s:>10} {row['peak_rate_units_s']!s:>10} {row['peak_accel_units_s2']!s:>11} \"",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:112:     max_speed = check_speed(args.max_speed, \"--max-speed\")",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:116:         rows = describe_plan(steps, poses, start=start, max_speed=max_speed, rate_hz=args.rate_hz)",
   "app/motion/run_sequence.py:135:             player = MotionPlayer(driver, max_speed=max_speed, rate_hz=args.rate_hz, tolerance=args.tolerance)",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:8: Limits: no move exceeds HARD_MAX_SPEED (50 units/s) or DEFAULT_MAX_ACCEL (50 units/s^2).",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:47: DEFAULT_MAX_SPEED = 25.0  # normalized units per second, all joints synchronized; tune on hardware",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:48: HARD_MAX_SPEED = 50.0  # ceiling for every speed (CLI, YAML, dry run and player); no override flag",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:49: DEFAULT_MAX_ACCEL = 50.0  # normalized units per second squared, peak of the smoothstep; tune on hardware",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:54: # Binding port rule (coordinator, 13:42Z): the follower is this by-id link. The Studio export's",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:56: FOLLOWER_PORT_BY_ID = \"/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_5B3D040939-if00\"",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:118:     \"\"\"Return value as a speed in units/s, or raise MotionError unless 0 < value <= HARD_MAX_SPEED.",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:121:         MotionError: If value is not a number, is not finite, is not positive or is above HARD_MAX_SPEED.",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:128:     if not (math.isfinite(speed) and 0.0 < speed <= HARD_MAX_SPEED):",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:129:         msg = f\"{label} must be above 0 and at most {HARD_MAX_SPEED:g} units/s, got {value!r}\"",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:161:     max_speed: float,",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:163:     max_accel: float = DEFAULT_MAX_ACCEL,",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:165:     \"\"\"Return setpoints that move every joint from start to target within the speed and acceleration limits.",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:169:     acceleration is 6 * delta / T^2. T = max(1.5 * delta / max_speed, sqrt(6 * delta / max_accel))",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:177:         MotionError: If max_speed, max_accel or dt is not finite and positive, or the shapes differ.",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:179:     if not (_finite_positive(max_speed) and _finite_positive(max_accel) and _finite_positive(dt)):",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:180:         msg = \"max_speed, max_accel and dt must be finite and positive\"",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:190:     duration = max(1.5 * delta / max_speed, math.sqrt(6.0 * delta / max_accel))",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:202:     The path is resolved first (a /dev/serial/by-id link becomes its /dev/ttyACM node), so the",
   "app/motion/so101_motion.py:324:     \"\"\"Connect with torque OFF so the arm can be moved by hand (teaching) or read only."
